## Authentication

All authentication is handled via `Authenticator` implementations passed to the client constructor.

### Credentials per security scheme

`{{clientClassName}}` takes one optional credential for each security scheme of the API, as a keyword argument named after the scheme{{#clientSchemes}}{{#-first}}: `{{/-first}}{{paramName}}{{^-last}}`, `{{/-last}}{{#-last}}`{{/-last}}{{/clientSchemes}}. Each operation uses the credential of the first scheme its spec lists that you configured; there is no per-call override. A single `authenticator` is the default for an operation none of whose schemes you configured, and a call with no matching credential and no default sends none. The client is refused (`ValueError`) when it gets no credential at all.

### Bearer Token

```python
from {{packageName}}.auth.bearer_authenticator import BearerAuthenticator

authenticator = BearerAuthenticator("https://api.example.com", "your-token")
client = {{clientClassName}}(authenticator)
```

